{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWordBlocks"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.threshold_to_pointwise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.threshold_to_pointwise","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.lean#L131-L148","doc":"**Threshold domination gives pointwise domination.**\n\nThe gap `TemperleyLiebWordBlocks` recorded, closed. Note that\n`J.card = I.card` — which `NormalIdx` does carry — is **not** needed: the\nthreshold condition alone forces the pointwise inequality wherever both lists\nhave an `r`-th entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.sorted_getElem_le_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.sorted_getElem_le_iff","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.lean#L90-L129","doc":"**The one lemma the bridge rests on.** For a strictly sorted list, \"the\n`r`-th entry is `≤ x`\" is exactly \"at least `r+1` entries are `≤ x`\".\n\nThe `¬ (a ≤ x)` branch is where sortedness is used: if the head already exceeds\n`x` then so does everything after it, so the filter is empty and both sides are\nfalse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.elems_filter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.elems_filter","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.lean#L81-L88","doc":"Filtering commutes with `elems`. Both sides are one `filter` over\n`List.finRange`, so this is `List.filter_filter` plus commutativity of `∧`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.elems_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.elems_length","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.lean#L72-L79","doc":"`elems` has exactly `s.card` entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.elems_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.elems_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge.lean#L68-L70","doc":"`elems` has no duplicates — inherited from `List.finRange` by `Sublist`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}